@Notes for developers: Use `GetlistingStatus` to search for ID for a list
@Note of script authors: Use `setlisting status" to change the status of a list in this script
Use: This script shows information about a list when you click on it. It also has a function that updates a property of a list by editing this property in the GUI or changing the value of a variable in a text block.
Right -click on a list entry. Select "List details" in the displayed menu. The menu is expanded and a list field full of listing details contains. You can then expand these elements as much as you would like to see detailed information. If you start double -clicking on something to get more information, you would like a "split window". Do this in the top left directly above the program icon. In this way you can display all open things in a single screen without returning to different windows, which is tedious.
